1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:02,055
How long to walk
to the Moon?

2
00:00:02,475 --> 00:00:04,790
Starting at your own
front door.

3
00:00:05,720 --> 00:00:08,810
The Moon sits
about 30 Earths away,

4
00:00:08,825 --> 00:00:10,985
lined up side by side,

5
00:00:10,985 --> 00:00:13,385
with nothing but
dark between.

6
00:00:14,120 --> 00:00:15,730
Walk at an easy pace,

7
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:17,625
the kind you
could chat through.

8
00:00:17,830 --> 00:00:20,080
Never stop,
not even to sleep.

9
00:00:20,310 --> 00:00:22,840
You would arrive
in about nine years.

10
00:00:23,720 --> 00:00:25,945
But nobody walks
day and night.

11
00:00:25,945 --> 00:00:28,920
You sleep, you eat,
you stop to tie a shoe.

12
00:00:29,080 --> 00:00:31,770
So give yourself a
working day of walking.

13
00:00:34,520 --> 00:00:36,600
A working day
of walking gets

14
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:39,290
you there
in about 26 years.

15
00:00:42,925 --> 00:00:45,610
Slower adds years,
quicker trims a few.

16
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:49,005
10,000 steps a day,
the popular goal,

17
00:00:49,005 --> 00:00:51,620
is only
about 7.5 kilometers.

18
00:00:52,285 --> 00:00:55,610
So that trip takes
about 140 years.

19
00:00:56,720 --> 00:00:58,745
Apollo eleven's crew
made

20
00:00:58,745 --> 00:01:01,270
the same trip
in about three days.

21
00:01:01,460 --> 00:01:04,705
The distance never
changed, only the speed.

22
00:01:09,792 --> 00:01:13,382
Real quick: like and follow. The next what-if is even stranger.
